  "note": "First election under the 1922 wards (North and South), polled 15 January 1923. W. J. Magowan withdrew in the North Ward, leaving six nominations for six seats; the South Ward had four nominations for six seats and the two retiring members, W. Cowan and J. Smith, were deemed re-elected. No contest took place in either ward (Northern Whig, 6 January 1923, p. 6; Belfast News-Letter, 9 January 1923, p. 6). E. and William Beatty were the retiring members. Returned unopposed."
